Changes to sing-box v1.14.4 (GNU GPL v3.0 or later), made by the unbraid authors, on 2026-11-17:
a stand-in (fake) address is never handed to a second name while the range is unchanged: once the range is used
up, lookups of new names are answered with a server failure instead, and libbox tells how many addresses are left
(FakeIPRemaining), so the app can move to a fresh range in time.
Applied by tools/build-libbox.sh; git apply skips these lines.

